te cancer
What changed
FDA approved talazoparib plus enzalutamide for patients with metastatic andro=
gen pathway modulation-na=C3=AFve or -sensitive prostate cancer carrying muta=
tions in any of 12 homologous-recombination-repair genes. In the 599-patient =
TALAPRO-3 trial, median radiographic progression-free survival was not reache=
d with the combination versus 45.8 months with enzalutamide alone, producing =
a hazard ratio of 0.48. Overall-survival data were immature. (
FDA,
FDA approves talazoparib with enzalutamide for metastatic androgen pathway mo=
dulation-na=C3=AFve or -sensitive prostate cancer
, October 26, 2026
)
What it tells us
The approval advances molecular selection and PARP inhibition from castration=
-resistant disease into the initial metastatic treatment architecture. The re=
lative effect is large, although the control arm=E2=80=99s 45.8-month median =
means absolute benefit and survival value will require longer follow-up. Comm=
ercial adoption will depend on routine tissue or circulating-tumor-DNA testin=
g and whether efficacy is consistent across the broad HRR-gene label. Myelosu=
ppression and the risks of MDS or acute myeloid leukemia add cumulative-treat=
ment considerations in a population that may remain on therapy for years.
What to watch next
Overall survival, gene-level subgroup results, treatment discontinuation and =
how clinicians position the combination relative to chemotherapy or androgen-=
receptor-pathway intensification.
4. Imetelstat=E2=80=99s myelofibrosis failure refutes its survival thesis
What changed
Geron discontinued the 327-patient Phase 3 IMpactMF trial after its independe=
nt monitoring committee concluded imetelstat was unlikely to improve overall =
survival versus best available therapy in JAK-inhibitor-relapsed or refractor=
y myelofibrosis. The committee identified no new safety issue. (
SEC/Geron,
Geron provides update on Phase 3 IMpactMF trial
, October 28, 2026
)
Earlier survival expectations relied partly on post hoc comparisons between t=
he single-arm IMbark study and matched real-world controls, rather than a ran=
domized survival comparison. (
Journal of Clinical Oncology,
Updated analysis of overall survival with imetelstat versus real-world data
, June 2026
